WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.559
Welcome to Module 2 of Defender
X D R Engineering and Operations:

2
00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:07.537
prevention and Attack Surface Reduction.

3
00:00:07.537 --> 00:00:11.610
A setting in a policy protects nothing
until it's enforced on the device,

4
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.475
and enforcing it all at once breaks
the applications nobody listed.

5
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:19.021
In this module you learn the
order of the prevention settings,

6
00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:23.749
which of them have an audit mode, how Attack
Surface Reduction moves through audit,

7
00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:26.460
warn and block, ring by
ring, and how to prove each

8
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.450
setting on the device rather
than trusting a report.

9
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.700
The module covers Steps 3 and 4 of the
Defender X D R implementation guide.

10
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.930
It takes about fifty minutes, plus
Lab 2 in your own test tenant.
